  1. Copy, reproduce or redistribute the contents, in whole or in part.
  2. Modify them or create derivative works based on them.
  3. Use them, in whole or in part, in other projects, academic work or
     course submissions.
  4. Publish, sell, sublicense or commercially exploit them.
  5. Use the game's names, title or branding.

The only things you may do are:

  - View the code and contents on GitHub, and fork them within GitHub, to
    the extent required by the GitHub Terms of Service. A fork does not
    grant any of the rights this licence withholds.
  - Play the builds published by the authors themselves (the .exe in the
    releases and the web version on GitHub Pages), for personal,
    non-commercial use only.

Third-party content: the sound effects and music come from Freesound (CC0),
and the Unity engine, packages and fonts are subject to their own licences.
This licence does not change the terms of that content.

To request permission, contact the authors through their GitHub profiles.

